# px93 (R-px93-9): the texts earlier installers wrote into the files an install generates, as
# `sha256 path`, each read from installs those installers made (px93's leg: 9c88ec8a's and 8b4e98ae's,
# the same two texts, px78's through 44b44435's). An upgrade writes a generated file again when it holds
# one of these; any other text but the new installer's is the user's, kept, the new text beside it as
# .pax-new. /etc/fstab and the root's limine.conf name the root's PARTUUID: the installer's template
# for the target's own PARTUUID is the only text written there, so no digest stands for them here. A
# change to installed_login() or INSTALLED_RUN (user/install/prepare.lu) keeps the old text's line.
# px106: px98's /etc/pax-login (c277b632 to px106's /bin/login: the installer's text since then) added,
# read by building trunk 7e65c2ce's installed_login() and hashing what it returns; /etc/pax-run's
# text did not change before px106.
85a48ba8f2bc23574469f965a60400debdc9bdeea9f850eb443a5953b52be188 /etc/pax-login
681996e130f41adea741315f7731522b39d762d9cfad14b64757cf63bddf149f /etc/pax-run
8a71588f2e8b19ce84a4893e0e0554f892258c86d2c56a202cffaa6050a7d751 /etc/pax-login
